==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|trānsdūcō}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|trāns-|gloss1=across, beyond|dūcō|gloss2=lead}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|trādūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|trādūcō}}

# to [[lead]], [[bring]], [[transport]] or [[conduct]] across or over something
#: {{syn|la|duco|deduco|produco|ago|veho|porto|perfero}}
# to [[parade]], lead along; [[make]] a [[show]] of, [[expose]] to [[public]] [[ridicule]]; [[dishonor]], [[disgrace]], [[degrade]]
#: {{syn|la|contemnō|spernō|abiciō|dēprimō|premō|lūdificō|rīdeō|ēlūdō}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[transfer]], [[convert]], [[remove]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[exhibit]], [[display]], [[proclaim]], [[spread]] abroad, make public
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[translate]] (transfer a [[word]] from one [[language]] to another)
# to [[derive]] (one word from another)
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of time}} to [[spend]], [[pass]], lead
#: {{syn|la|dēgō|terō|cōnsūmō|trānsmittō|eximō|tollō|agō}}

